      "writtenOn": "2021-12-20T12:08:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why specifically this class ? Are you by any chance trying to provide guarantees of iteration order ? If so, why ? Be careful of Hyrum\u0027s law.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 602,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 602,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "5beccee91566e8bca78f10f18d88623f21f34510",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9e6f1d8a_47ee1276",
        "filename": "packages/ConnectivityT/framework-t/src/android/net/NetworkTemplate.java",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 602,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-12-20T15:10:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes.\nThe reason for this is we still rely on the first IMSI to be the major one,\ne.g. normalize(...) {\n   ...\n   new NetworkTemplate(template.mMatchRule, merged[0], merged,\n                        template.mNetworkId); \n}\n                        \nIIUC that means our internal implementation should have stable order of IMSIs.\nOtherwise, each time we call normalize() might result in a different template.\n\nIIUC this can be resolved after we remove all single IMSI logic in NPMS.\nBut for now it seems to me can: \n  1. Make sure the order is deterministic.\n  2. Or, use SortedSet which always choose the same IMSI among multiple IMSIs. e.g. smallest.\nIIUC either way suffers from Hyrum\u0027s law.\n  \nSimilar to normalize()\nCurrently, most of the callers currently only support single SIM, e.g. NPMS.\nIf we don\u0027t provide a stable order, then:\n 1. What should we return if the caller tried to get a single IMSI among multiple IMSIs, (l.593)?\n 2. If the caller calls build() twice with multiple IMSI, the result NetworkTemplate might be differed. (before we remove the signle IMSI variable in NetworkTemplate)",
      "parentUuid": "3d30b9e2_d57b6382",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 602,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 602,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "5beccee91566e8bca78f10f18d88623f21f34510",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
